! MCP INITIALIZATION, printed p.61 (MCP_Mar63_001-249 PDF p.68) --
! THE ASSIGN PROGRAM'S CONSTANTS AND INDEX NAMES.
!
! Fifty-six lines, of which TWENTY compile a word.  The rest are
! comments and SYN cards, and the SYN cards are most of the page:
! lines 13-14 and 31-47 define the ASSIGN program's symbol set.
!
! The listing's own headings divide it:
!   lines  3-5   "CONSTANTS TO BE USED THRU OUT ASSIGN PROGRAM"
!   lines 11-12  "THE FORMAT OF THE TEMP CHAN WORD"
!   lines 48-50  "SAVE AREAS FOR INDEXES"
!   lines 54-56  "SYN CARDS FOR THE PP REFERENCE TABLE"  (the cards
!                themselves are on printed p.62)
!
! >>> IT RUNS STRAIGHT INTO printed p.62. <<<  Line 52 is
! "T ASAVE DRZ(BU,64),(15)" at 003274.00 -- fifteen words -- ending
! at 003313.00, which is printed p.62 line 2.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> ONE ROW CONFIRMS printed p.60's SYN CARDS FROM THIS PAGE'S
! OWN BINARY <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 19 is "T SAV  XW,T PREFT,T PPC,T PPREF" and compiles
!
!     003317.00+ 000 000024 003314
!
! -- an XW's four groups are value, flags, count and refill.  THE
! COUNT IS 000024 = 20 DECIMAL, which is exactly what printed p.60
! line 6 declares: "T PPC  SYN,20", printed there with `NULL` in the
! binary column because a SYN compiles nothing.  p.60 says the number
! and p.61 spends it, one page apart.
!
! And the same row fixes two addresses on the NEXT page: T PREFT is
! 003317.0 and T PPREF is 003314.0, both on printed p.62.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A VF WITH AN EMPTY VALUE FIELD, AND THE MANUAL SAYS WHAT IT DOES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 7 is "T NEXT  VF," -- a comma and nothing after it -- and
! compiles 000000.00+.  C22-6531 printed p.7: "A NULL FIELD IS ALWAYS
! COMPILED AS A ZERO."  The same rule already covers an XW with no
! operands at all (lines 8, 16, 17 and 18, each 000000.00+ 000 000000
! 000000), so this page uses it in both shapes on one page.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TEN ONE-BIT DATA DEFINITIONS IN ONE WORD, AND THE ADDRESSES COUNT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 20 is "T LUCT DD(BU,18),0" at 003273.00, and lines 21-30 are
! ten "DD(BU,1)" rows at 003273.22, .23, .24, .25, .26, .27, .30,
! .31, .32 and .33 -- consecutive OCTAL bit offsets, which is 18
! through 27 in decimal.  Eighteen bits of T LUCT then one bit each.
! A page where the location column alone proves every field width.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! CNOP COMPILES A HALF WORD, AND IT IS NOT ALIGNMENT ALONE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 51 is a bare "CNOP" at 003273.40 compiling 000000.30 00.  The
! counter stood at 003273.34 after line 30's last one-bit DD, so the
! CNOP both ROUNDED UP to the half word AND emitted an instruction.
! That is the same pseudo-operation whose ABSENCE from
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p7_p8.strap was found on 2026-10-23, when
! correcting VF's size from a half word to its documented
! twenty-five bits made printed p.8 line 31 miss by five bits.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE INDEX NAMES, AND THE LOCATION COLUMN PRINTS THE REGISTER
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 31-47 are seventeen SYN cards aliasing index registers, and
! on a SYN row the LOCATION column prints the RESOLVED VALUE.  Each
! resolves to the index register's WORD address, 16+n:
!
!   000021 = $1    000025 = $5    000031 = $9
!   000022 = $2    000026 = $6    000032 = $10
!   000023 = $3    000027 = $7
!   000024 = $4    000030 = $8
!
! so "T X1BR SYN,$1" prints 000021.00+ and "T X1 SYN,$10" prints
! 000032.00+.  SEVEN OF THE SEVENTEEN ALIAS ANOTHER ALIAS rather
! than a register -- T CTWDX, T IXF, T IXK and T IXL are SYN,T X1;
! T IXH is SYN,T X3; T IXI is SYN,T IXB; T IXM is SYN,T IXG -- and
! each resolves to the same word as the name it points at, which is
! C22-6531 printed p.31's "EXACT SUBSTITUTION" applied twice over.
!
! A SYN WITH A dds PRINTS THAT dds IN THE BINARY COLUMN.  Lines 13
! and 14 print "BU,22 ,10" and "BU,07 ,10" -- length 0o22 = 18 and
! 0o07 = 7, byte size 0o10 = 8 -- against statements that read
! "SYN(BU,18),T CTEMP+0.0" and "SYN(BU,7),T CTEMP+0.25".  The
! location column gives 003265.00+ and 003265.31+, and 0o31 = 25,
! so the expression and the dds check each other.
!
! TWO LISTING MARKS: lines 7 ("003264.40 *" -- the page's first
! compiled row) and 52 ("003274.00 *").

        SLC, (8)3264.40

! ---- external: printed p.60's SYN cards and p.62's tables ---------
TPPC    SYN, 20
TPREFT  SYN, (8)3317.0
TPPREF  SYN, (8)3314.0

        SLC, (8)3264.40

! ---- CONSTANTS TO BE USED THRU OUT ASSIGN PROGRAM ------------------
TNEXT   VF,                          ! line 7  -THE ADDR OF THE NEXT
                                      !           PP TO BE RUN
TCTEMP  XW                           ! line 8  -TEMP SYMBOLIC CHAN
                                      !           WORD
TIPL    VF, 0.0                      ! line 9  -CHAN ADDRESSES FOR IPL

! ---- THE FORMAT OF THE TEMP CHAN WORD ------------------------------
TCTACH  SYN(BU,18), TCTEMP+0.0       ! line 13 -ABSOLUTE CHANNEL
                                      !           NUMBER
TCTSCH  SYN(BU,7), TCTEMP+0.25       ! line 14 -SYMBOLIC CHANNEL
                                      !           NUMBER

TWORK1  XW                           ! line 16 -TEMPORARY WORKING WORD
TWORK2  XW                           ! line 17 -TEMPORARY WORKING WORD
TREFIL  XW                           ! line 18 -TEMP STORAGE FOR IX -A-
TSAV    XW, TPREFT, TPPC, TPPREF     ! line 19
TLUCT   DD(BU,18), 0                 ! line 20 -LARGEST UNIT COUNT ON
                                      !           ONE CHANNEL
TONE    DD(BU,1), 1                  ! line 21 -CONSTANT OF ONE
TMODE   DD(BU,1), 0                  ! line 22 -SINGLE OR FULL
                                      !           NOT-OVERLAP MODE
TINDA   DD(BU,1), 0                  ! line 23 -SAME CHANNEL ALLOWED
                                      !           INDICATOR
TINDB   DD(BU,1), 0                  ! line 24 -THE SPLIT CHANNEL
                                      !           INDICATOR
TINDC   DD(BU,1), 0                  ! line 25 -UNIT FOUND --
                                      !           MULTI-UNIT CHECK
TINDD   DD(BU,1), 0                  ! line 26 -BYPASS OPTIMISED REEL
                                      !           MTINGS
TINDE   DD(BU,1), 0                  ! line 27 -THE ADVANCE AND SAVE
                                      !           INDEX IND
TINDZ   DD(BU,1), 0                  ! line 28 -MORE MULTI-UNITS
                                      !           AVAILABLE
TLOOP   DD(BU,1), 0                  ! line 29 -TO PREVENT A LOOP IN
                                      !           SECTION ELEVEN
TLOOP1  DD(BU,1), 0                  ! line 30 -LOOP PREVENTER NUMBER 2

! ---- the index names ----------------------------------------------
TCTWDX  SYN, TX1                     ! line 31 -ENTRY CONTROL WORD
                                      !           INDEX
TX1     SYN, $10                     ! line 32 -TEMPORARY INDEX
TX2     SYN, $9                      ! line 33 -THE SCAN CONTROL INDEX
TX1BR   SYN, $1                      ! line 34 -FOR SUB-ROUTINE
                                      !           BRANCHING
TX3     SYN, $2                      ! line 35 -COUNTER
TIXA    SYN, $4                      ! line 36 -I/O REQ. LOCATOR INDEX
TIXB    SYN, $5                      ! line 37 -MULTI-UNIT STAT TBLE
                                      !           SCAN INDEX
TIXE    SYN, $3                      ! line 38 -PP REF. WORD LOCATOR
                                      !           INDEX
TIXF    SYN, TX1                     ! line 39 -MACH CONF CHANGE--
                                      !           CHAN. SCAN IX
TIXG    SYN, $8                      ! line 40 -MACH CONF CHANGE --
                                      !           UNIT SCAN
TIXH    SYN, TX3                     ! line 41 -MACH CONF CHANGE --
                                      !           PP REF TBL SCAN
TIXI    SYN, TIXB                    ! line 42 -MACH CONF CHANGE --
                                      !           I/O TBLE SCAN IX
TIXJ    SYN, $6                      ! line 43 -UNIT TBLE ADDR. AND
                                      !           UNIT COUNT
TIXD    SYN, $7                      ! line 44 -CHANNEL ADDRESS
TIXK    SYN, TX1                     ! line 45 -LIKE CHANNEL SEARCH
                                      !           INDEX
TIXL    SYN, TX1                     ! line 46 -I/O TABLE SCAN INDEX
TIXM    SYN, TIXG                    ! line 47 -NOT OVERLAP SCANNER
                                      !           INDEX

! ---- SAVE AREAS FOR INDEXES ----------------------------------------
        CNOP                         ! line 51
TASAVE  DRZ(BU,64), (15)             ! line 52 -AREA SET ASIDE FOR
                                      !           INDEX SAVING
        END, TNEXT

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKED ROWS -- the twenty that compile a word.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  7  003264.40  000000.00+                        T NEXT  VF,
!   line  8  003265.00  000000.00+ 000 000000 000000      T CTEMP XW
!   line  9  003266.00  000000.00+                        T IPL   VF,0.0
!   line 16  003267.00  000000.00+ 000 000000 000000      T WORK1 XW
!   line 17  003270.00  000000.00+ 000 000000 000000      T WORK2 XW
!   line 18  003271.00  000000.00+ 000 000000 000000      T REFIL XW
!   line 19  003272.00  003317.00+ 000 000024 003314      T SAV   XW
!   line 20  003273.00  000000                            T LUCT  DD(BU,18)
!   line 21  003273.22  1                                 T ONE   DD(BU,1),1
!   line 22  003273.23  0                                 T MODE
!   line 23  003273.24  0                                 T INDA
!   line 24  003273.25  0                                 T INDB
!   line 25  003273.26  0                                 T INDC
!   line 26  003273.27  0                                 T INDD
!   line 27  003273.30  0                                 T INDE
!   line 28  003273.31  0                                 T INDZ
!   line 29  003273.32  0                                 T LOOP
!   line 30  003273.33  0                                 T LOOP1
!   line 51  003273.40  000000.30 00                      CNOP
!   line 52  003274.00  000017.00                         T ASAVE DRZ(15)
